      "text": [
        " يُسْتَحَبُّ أَنْ يَكُونَ فِي كَفَنِهِ ثَوْبٌ كَانَ يُصَلِّي فِيهِ نَظِيفٌ فَإِنَّ ذَلِكَ يُسْتَحَبُّ أَنْ يُكَفَّنَ فِيمَا كَانَ يُصَلِّي فِيهِ ."
      ],
      "translations": {
        "en.hubeali": [
          "Ali Bin Ibrahim, from his father, from Abdullah Bin Al Mugheira, from one of his companions who said, ",
          "‘It is recommended that there happens to be in his shroud a (piece of cloth) which he used to pray <span class=\"iTxt\">Salaat</span> in, clean, for that is recommended that you enshroud him in what he used to pray <span class=\"iTxt\">Salaat</span> in’."
        ],
        "en.sarwar": [
          "4. Ali ibn Ibrahim has narrated from his father from ‘Abd Allah ibn al-Mughirah from certain persons of his people who has said the following: “He (the Imam), ‘Alayhi al-Salam, has said, ‘It is desirable to keep for shroud a piece which one has used in Salah (prayer). It should be clean; it is desirable.”’ "
        ]
      }
